We're hiring Lead React / TypeScript Developers!

Terms: 12 + 12 month contract - 37.5hrs per week
Clearance: NV1 Security Clearance required 
About: Lead the design, development & delivery of complex React & TypeScript applications

Our client, an independent Federal Government agency responsible for implementing and administering the National Disability Insurance Scheme, require the services of a Lead React & TypeScript Developer.

Duties:
Lead the design, development & delivery of modern web applications using React, TypeScript & contemporary frontend engineering practices;
Provide technical leadership, mentoring & guidance to development team members, establishing engineering standards & promoting high-quality delivery outcomes;
Collaborate with business stakeholders, UX designers, architects & backend development teams to define frontend requirements, API contracts & end-to-end solution designs;
Drive the adoption of modern software engineering practices, including AI-assisted development, automated testing, source control, CI/CD pipelines & Agile delivery methodologies.

Skills and Experience Required:
Demonstrated experience leading the design, development & delivery of complex React & TypeScript applications in an enterprise environment;
Strong technical expertise across modern frontend development, including React, TypeScript, component-based architecture, state management, API integration & responsive user interface design;
Demonstrated experience delivering accessible digital services and implementing accessibility standards & best practices, with a strong understanding of inclusive design principles;
Experience establishing engineering standards & practices, including code review, automated testing, CI/CD pipelines, source control & release management;
Demonstrated experience leveraging contemporary AI-assisted software engineering tools (such as agentic coding assistants, code generation, automated testing & code review capabilities) to accelerate software delivery, improve quality & support modern development practices;
Experience delivering applications using modern frontend ecosystems and tooling, including TypeScript, API-driven architectures, component libraries, cloud-native platforms & contemporary development frameworks (desired);
Experience working with specification-driven or AI-augmented software development approaches, including the use of structured requirements, design artefacts & automated tooling to accelerate delivery & improve quality (desired).

